WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.791
<b>Without any attachment to the fruit, performing </b>
<b>selfless Karma Yoga (Nishkam Karma Yoga), </b>

2
00:00:33.791 --> 00:00:40.000
<b>and also dedicating the result of the action</b>
<b>towards God, towards the welfare of society,</b>

3
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.500
<b>this is the path to unite with the Supreme Soul,</b>

4
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.791
<b>to be free from the bondage of sin and virtue.</b>

5
00:00:46.791 --> 00:00:50.416
<b>But it is natural for the question </b>
<b>to arise in the human mind,</b>

6
00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:53.041
<b>that all this seems very difficult,</b>

7
00:00:53.041 --> 00:00:59.875
<b>is there no way to make this life happy </b>
<b>while living with worldly attachments?</b>

8
00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:04.291
<b>The very remedies for that are </b>
<b>mentioned in these two verses.</b>

9
00:01:04.291 --> 00:01:07.541
<b>These remedies can make life happy,</b>

10
00:01:07.541 --> 00:01:09.333
<b>can purify the mind,</b>

11
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:14.583
<b>and ultimately can also lead man </b>
<b>towards selfless Karma Yoga.</b>

12
00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:21.291
<b>In these verses, Lord Krishna tells</b>

13
00:01:21.291 --> 00:01:23.416
<b>that at the time of the creation of this universe,</b>

14
00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:29.041
<b>its creator, Prajapati Brahma, gave man </b>
<b>a system of Yagya and said</b>

15
00:01:29.041 --> 00:01:32.291
<b>- by performing this Yagya, </b>
<b>you can attain prosperity,</b>

16
00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:35.875
<b>this Yagya will become the </b>
<b>means of fulfilling your desires.</b>

17
00:01:35.875 --> 00:01:39.291
<b>By offering oblations to the Yagya, </b>
<b>you will please the gods,</b>

18
00:01:39.291 --> 00:01:43.458
<b>and in return those gods will fulfill your desires.</b>

19
00:01:43.458 --> 00:01:48.583
<b>By this mutual relationship, you will be </b>
<b>able to attain the highest welfare.</b>

20
00:01:48.583 --> 00:01:52.500
<b>Lord Krishna wants to say that </b>
<b>the person who has desires,</b>

21
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.541
<b>and is not capable of </b>
<b>performing selfless Karma Yoga,</b>

22
00:01:55.541 --> 00:02:00.291
<b>should perform such Yagya-like actions </b>
<b>according to the scriptures,</b>

23
00:02:00.291 --> 00:02:01.666
<b>this will give happiness,</b>

24
00:02:01.666 --> 00:02:07.083
<b>and man should also continuously do</b>
<b>his spiritual development along with it.</b>

25
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:10.083
<b>Pleasing the gods by Yagya-like actions,</b>

26
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:14.291
<b>and in return the gods fulfilling the desires of man,</b>

27
00:02:14.291 --> 00:02:20.583
<b>this is similar to how man pays his</b>
<b>taxes to the government administration,</b>

28
00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:28.333
<b>and in return the administration provides </b>
<b>him with electricity, water, roads, etc. facilities.</b>

29
00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:30.166
<b>The only difference is,</b>

30
00:02:30.166 --> 00:02:33.958
<b>the relationship between government </b>
<b>administration and citizens</b>

31
00:02:33.958 --> 00:02:36.833
<b>runs the country smoothly,</b>

32
00:02:36.833 --> 00:02:44.916
<b>while this exchange between gods and </b>
<b>man keeps the entire universe progressive.</b>

33
00:02:44.916 --> 00:02:48.083
<b>Just as in the administration of a country</b>
<b>there are many departments,</b>

34
00:02:48.083 --> 00:02:48.958
<b>for electricity,</b>

35
00:02:48.958 --> 00:02:49.750
<b>water,</b>

36
00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.041
<b>roads etc.,</b>

37
00:02:52.041 --> 00:02:55.750
<b>similarly in the universe also </b>
<b>there are energy department,</b>

38
00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:57.833
<b>under the management of Sun God,</b>

39
00:02:57.833 --> 00:03:01.708
<b>education department, under the </b>
<b>management of Goddess Saraswati,</b>

40
00:03:01.708 --> 00:03:04.791
<b>fire department, under the </b>
<b>management of Fire God</b>

41
00:03:04.791 --> 00:03:07.916
<b>and many such departments.</b>

42
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.708
<b>How beautiful is the creation of this universe,</b>

43
00:03:17.708 --> 00:03:22.916
<b>where if everyone just keeps </b>
<b>doing their assigned actions,</b>

44
00:03:22.916 --> 00:03:27.916
<b>lives a life of gratitude and cooperation,</b>

45
00:03:27.916 --> 00:03:31.208
<b>then everyone will attain prosperity.</b>

46
00:03:31.208 --> 00:03:33.458
<b>No one will be left behind.</b>

47
00:03:33.458 --> 00:03:37.333
<b>Man will only have to understand</b>

48
00:03:37.333 --> 00:03:43.333
<b>that to remain happy he </b>
<b>needs mutual cooperation,</b>

49
00:03:43.333 --> 00:03:46.583
<b>he needs others,</b>

50
00:03:46.583 --> 00:03:51.708
<b>he has no existence alone.</b>

51
00:03:51.708 --> 00:03:54.666
<b>Gratitude and mutual cooperation,</b>

52
00:03:54.666 --> 00:03:59.875
<b>these two qualities are the </b>
<b>fundamental pillars of this universe.</b>

53
00:03:59.875 --> 00:04:00.833
<b>And</b>

54
00:04:00.833 --> 00:04:07.500
<b>there is a need to bring these </b>
<b>principles into personal life as well.</b>

55
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:18.666
<b>When a person is always grateful for this life, </b>
<b>and for the role of others in shaping this life,</b>

56
00:04:18.666 --> 00:04:21.208
<b>then it means</b>

57
00:04:21.208 --> 00:04:26.125
<b>that there is no negativity in his mind.</b>

58
00:04:26.125 --> 00:04:27.708
<b>Rather,</b>

59
00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:32.500
<b>he is looking at life only from </b>
<b>the perspective of prosperity.</b>

60
00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.416
<b>Where he has everything</b>

61
00:04:36.416 --> 00:04:39.416
<b>Sufficient means, good-bad experiences,</b>

62
00:04:39.416 --> 00:04:43.750
<b>everything is only for his good.</b>

63
00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.666
<b>And a person with such a prosperous attitude</b>

64
00:04:47.666 --> 00:04:51.083
<b>does not feel jealous of others,</b>

65
00:04:51.083 --> 00:04:53.833
<b>he helps others.</b>

66
00:04:53.833 --> 00:04:54.791
<b>And</b>

67
00:04:54.791 --> 00:05:04.375
<b>in return for this help, he also gets help</b>
<b>and good wishes at every turn.</b>

68
00:05:04.375 --> 00:05:07.291
<b>What a beautiful cycle this is.</b>

69
00:05:07.291 --> 00:05:12.833
<b>Where the feeling of </b>
<b>gratitude inspires cooperation,</b>

70
00:05:12.833 --> 00:05:16.375
<b>cooperation brings prosperity,</b>

71
00:05:16.375 --> 00:05:22.500
<b>and man is again grateful for that prosperity.</b>

72
00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:23.916
<b>No jealousy,</b>

73
00:05:23.916 --> 00:05:25.666
<b>no malice.</b>

74
00:05:25.666 --> 00:05:28.125
<b>Only everyone's progress.</b>

75
00:05:28.125 --> 00:05:31.208
<b>Life is like a mirror.</b>

76
00:05:31.208 --> 00:05:38.041
<b>What you give, that will be returned </b>
<b>to you in life like a reflection.</b>

77
00:05:38.041 --> 00:05:39.458
<b>Therefore,</b>

78
00:05:39.458 --> 00:05:41.541
<b>always be grateful,</b>

79
00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:44.458
<b>always cooperate with others.</b>

80
00:05:44.458 --> 00:05:46.083
<b>In return,</b>

81
00:05:46.083 --> 00:05:50.375
<b>you will also get this.</b>

82
00:05:50.375 --> 00:05:54.083
<b>Life will be blissful.</b>

83
00:05:54.083 --> 00:05:56.041
<b>Think about it.</b>

84
00:06:00.833 --> 00:06:04.541
<b>In social situations,</b>

85
00:06:04.541 --> 00:06:07.125
<b>there are generally three types of people.</b>

86
00:06:07.125 --> 00:06:08.416
<b>One, those</b>

87
00:06:08.416 --> 00:06:12.041
<b>who are completely dependent on others.</b>

88
00:06:12.041 --> 00:06:13.791
<b>In any relationship,</b>

89
00:06:13.791 --> 00:06:19.000
<b>these people rely only on </b>
<b>the initiative of others, their help.</b>

90
00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.791
<b>They only know how to receive,</b>

91
00:06:21.791 --> 00:06:23.750
<b>not to give.</b>

92
00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.041
<b>On the contrary,</b>

93
00:06:25.041 --> 00:06:26.291
<b>there are also</b>

94
00:06:26.291 --> 00:06:28.750
<b>those who are completely solitary.</b>

95
00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:35.791
<b>Their belief is that they do not need </b>
<b>anyone else for happiness in life.</b>

96
00:06:35.791 --> 00:06:38.958
<b>They may certainly help,</b>

97
00:06:38.958 --> 00:06:44.250
<b>but they reject any help extended towards them.</b>

98
00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:49.833
<b>In both these situations, relationships </b>
<b>do not last for long.</b>

99
00:06:49.833 --> 00:06:57.291
<b>A relationship with a subordinate </b>
<b>person soon becomes a heavy burden.</b>

100
00:06:57.291 --> 00:06:59.166
<b>Where there is no cooperation,</b>

101
00:06:59.166 --> 00:07:01.500
<b>only dependence.</b>

102
00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.208
<b>On the other hand,</b>

103
00:07:03.208 --> 00:07:08.166
<b>people who consider themselves </b>
<b>completely independent,</b>

104
00:07:08.166 --> 00:07:14.541
<b>inadvertently make others feel </b>
<b>dependent on them.</b>

105
00:07:14.541 --> 00:07:21.041
<b>The balance gets disturbed </b>
<b>in such relationships as well.</b>

106
00:07:21.041 --> 00:07:24.833
<b>The foundation of sweet relationships is balance.</b>

107
00:07:24.833 --> 00:07:31.375
<b>An equation where both people </b>
<b>are desirous of cooperation,</b>

108
00:07:31.375 --> 00:07:33.458
<b>and also provide assistance.</b>

109
00:07:33.458 --> 00:07:37.208
<b>These are the third type of people,</b>

110
00:07:37.208 --> 00:07:42.208
<b>who neither consider themselves completely </b>
<b>dependent on someone,</b>

111
00:07:42.208 --> 00:07:45.666
<b>nor completely independent.</b>

112
00:07:45.666 --> 00:07:47.166
<b>They know that</b>

113
00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:49.875
<b>according to life's circumstances,</b>

114
00:07:49.875 --> 00:07:59.500
<b>they will give cooperation, and when needed, they </b>
<b>will also not be ashamed to accept cooperation.</b>

115
00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:03.541
<b>Understand the importance </b>
<b>of this cooperation in life.</b>

116
00:08:03.541 --> 00:08:06.083
<b>Adopt this perspective.</b>

117
00:08:06.083 --> 00:08:10.708
<b>Only such relationships are mutually sustained.</b>

118
00:08:10.708 --> 00:08:12.416
<b>Think about it.</b>

119
00:08:17.083 --> 00:08:19.250
<b>The progress of any organization</b>

120
00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:23.416
<b>depends on the satisfaction of its customers,</b>

121
00:08:23.416 --> 00:08:24.666
<b>and</b>

122
00:08:24.666 --> 00:08:26.625
<b>this satisfaction depends</b>

123
00:08:26.625 --> 00:08:30.916
<b>on the quality of the products of that organization.</b>

124
00:08:30.916 --> 00:08:37.708
<b>Many people work together with the goal </b>
<b>of improving this quality.</b>

125
00:08:37.708 --> 00:08:39.958
<b>Think about it</b>

126
00:08:39.958 --> 00:08:43.375
<b>- who does not like sweet music</b>

127
00:08:43.375 --> 00:08:44.833
<b>A music in which</b>

128
00:08:44.833 --> 00:08:55.458
<b>- sitar, tabla, flute and many such instruments</b>
<b>come together to produce a sweet sound.</b>

129
00:08:55.458 --> 00:09:01.416
<b>The only purpose of this harmony </b>
<b>is the joy of the listeners.</b>

130
00:09:01.416 --> 00:09:02.583
<b>But</b>

131
00:09:02.583 --> 00:09:04.833
<b>if, one day,</b>

132
00:09:04.833 --> 00:09:06.875
<b>the tabla, or the flute,</b>

133
00:09:06.875 --> 00:09:10.666
<b>or any other instrument becomes selfish,</b>

134
00:09:10.666 --> 00:09:15.291
<b>and in this selfishness starts</b>
<b>sounding louder than the others,</b>

135
00:09:15.291 --> 00:09:19.791
<b>then the entire music will be spoiled.</b>

136
00:09:19.791 --> 00:09:23.750
<b>The selfishness of any one instrument</b>

137
00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:28.125
<b>can ruin the entire musical composition.</b>

138
00:09:28.125 --> 00:09:29.833
<b>Similarly,</b>

139
00:09:29.833 --> 00:09:37.458
<b>the product of any organization depends on the</b>
<b>proportion of cooperation of many colleagues.</b>

140
00:09:37.458 --> 00:09:42.291
<b>But if some of these people </b>
<b>leave the collective goal</b>

141
00:09:42.291 --> 00:09:46.791
<b>and start getting motivated only</b>
<b>by personal selfishness,</b>

142
00:09:46.791 --> 00:09:49.166
<b>then cooperation will become difficult.</b>

143
00:09:49.166 --> 00:09:51.166
<b>The proportion will be reversed,</b>

144
00:09:51.166 --> 00:09:55.375
<b>and this will reduce the quality of the products.</b>

145
00:09:55.375 --> 00:09:58.416
<b>Consumers will reject it.</b>

146
00:09:58.416 --> 00:10:04.208
<b>Just as the excess of any one </b>
<b>ingredient in food spoils the taste,</b>

147
00:10:04.208 --> 00:10:05.458
<b>similarly</b>

148
00:10:05.458 --> 00:10:11.458
<b>the selfish nature of some </b>
<b>people can harm the organization.</b>

149
00:10:11.458 --> 00:10:19.875
<b>Therefore, any organization should encourage </b>
<b>not negative competition,</b>

150
00:10:19.875 --> 00:10:20.833
<b>but</b>

151
00:10:20.833 --> 00:10:24.333
<b>positive cooperation among people</b>
<b>and different departments.</b>

152
00:10:24.333 --> 00:10:26.291
<b>Only this will lead to progress.</b>

153
00:10:26.291 --> 00:10:31.000
<b>And this responsibility is also on </b>
<b>the people working there,</b>

154
00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:36.666
<b>if they will work by renouncing selfishness, </b>
<b>with cooperation, then there will be development,</b>

155
00:10:36.666 --> 00:10:40.583
<b>and they will also get the benefit </b>
<b>of this development.</b>

156
00:10:40.583 --> 00:10:47.625
<b>This is an equation of mutual participation </b>
<b>between the organization and the employees.</b>

157
00:10:47.625 --> 00:10:50.375
<b>This is the path of progress.</b>

158
00:10:50.375 --> 00:10:52.125
<b>Think about it.</b>

